#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:1
msgid "The filing workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:3
msgid ""
"This page covers the filing workflow's two building blocks - the work "
"unit (the saved workspace for one filing target) and the calculation "
"revision (one saved calculation result) - and how create, calculate, "
"verify, file, and export choose between them. Use it after completing the"
" quickstart if you want to understand how the tool organises and stores "
"your filing work between steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:10
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:12
msgid "You need an active profile, and the tool needs your master-key passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:14
msgid ""
"Create a profile first if you do not have one (see [Set up your taxpayer "
"profile](profile-setup.md)). Pass `--quiet` for the non-interactive form "
"(a bare `profile create NAME` opens an interactive wizard). A profile "
"that will reach `export` must carry a name and surnames, or `export` "
"refuses with \"requires the operator name\":"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:23
msgid ""
"Every profile-scoped command needs the master-key passphrase; the tool "
"prompts for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:26
msgid "The CLI emits help, results, and refusals in Spanish."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:28
msgid "The filing chain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:30
msgid ""
"The command-line interface is the same one used in the quickstart. Run "
"the four commands in order, from the profile above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:37
msgid ""
"The `--activity-start-date` in the profile above scopes out the prior-"
"period dependency for this first filing, so `verify` reports `complete` "
"and `export` writes the `.boe`. Without it, `verify` blocks on an "
"unresolved cross-period dependency on the prior period and `export` "
"refuses. To file a period that folds in a real prior period, import that "
"prior filing's evidence first; see [Reconcile a filing](reconcile.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:44
msgid ""
"`--modelo`, `--year`, and `--period` are the normal way to name the "
"filing you are working on. Use that shape for routine create, calculate, "
"verify, file, export, status, history, and revision commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:48
msgid "Start with the visible filing target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:50
msgid "A filing target is the filing as you see it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:52
msgid "the active profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:53
msgid "the modelo code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:54
msgid "the filing year"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:55
msgid "the period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:57
msgid ""
"For example, `--modelo 303 --year 2026 --period 1T` means \"Modelo 303, "
"first quarter of 2026, for the active profile.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:60
msgid "That same visible target works across the normal workflow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:66
msgid ""
"If no saved work exists yet, create it first with `aeat app modelo work "
"create` (the chain and visible-target sequences above run the full form)."
" Running the same create command again does not create a duplicate. It "
"returns the existing saved work for that filing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:71
msgid "How a filing gets its ID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:73
msgid ""
"The tool assigns a unique reference number to each filing workspace. For "
"most use you do not need to know or remember it. The tool finds your work"
" automatically from the modelo, year, and period you type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:77
msgid ""
"The tool knows which version of the official tax rules applies to each "
"form and period. You do not need to choose this manually. Use "
"`--revision` only when support or an error message asks you to target a "
"specific ruleset version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:81
msgid "To see the reference number for a saved filing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:87
msgid "After you have the `work_unit_id`, address the same saved work by ID:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:92
msgid ""
"Prefer the visible target for hand-run commands. Use the reference number"
" when Cadrumo reports that more than one filing matches the same modelo, "
"year, and period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:95
msgid "A work unit is one filing in progress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:97
msgid ""
"A work unit is the saved workspace for one filing target. It is the thing"
" that connects later commands to the same local filing work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:100
msgid ""
"For example, `aeat app modelo work create` creates or reuses the work "
"unit for Modelo 303 Q1 2026 (the chain sequence above runs the full "
"form)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:103
msgid "The tool keeps a record of your filing work. That record links to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:105
msgid "the latest calculated draft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:106
msgid "the verified draft, if you have verified one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:107
msgid "the filed record, if you have marked one as filed locally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:109
msgid ""
"No separate command \"switches\" the current work unit. The active "
"profile is global, but the filing work is selected on each command. To "
"work on a different filing, pass a different visible target or pass a "
"different `work_unit_id`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:116
msgid "A calculation revision is one saved result"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:118
msgid ""
"A calculation revision is one saved calculation result inside a work "
"unit. It has its own reference number, the calculation-revision-id, which"
" `calculate` creates and which is separate from the work-unit-id."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:122
msgid ""
"When you run `aeat app modelo work calculate`, Cadrumo saves a draft "
"calculation revision (the chain sequence above runs it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:125
msgid ""
"Running calculation again does not overwrite the old result. Every saved "
"calculation is immutable: earlier revisions stay on disk exactly as they "
"were, identified by their exact contents, so you can compare revisions "
"and go back. If your transactions or manual values changed, the tool "
"creates a new saved calculation alongside the old; if nothing changed, it"
" reuses the same result. The tool updates your filing record to reflect "
"the latest calculated draft. A saved revision is a record of one attempt,"
" not a verdict"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:132
msgid "its numbers commit to nothing until you verify and file it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:134
msgid ""
"List the saved calculation revisions for a filing with `aeat app modelo "
"work revisions`, and show the current revision's persisted values with "
"`aeat app modelo work revision` (the visible-target sequence above runs "
"both)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:138
msgid ""
"If you need to view one specific saved calculation, type its reference "
"number after the command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:144
msgid "Reference numbers to know:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:146
msgid "the filing workspace reference - from `aeat app modelo work list`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:147
msgid "the saved calculation reference - from `aeat app modelo work revisions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:148
msgid "the rules version reference - shown in status output; you rarely need this"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:149
msgid "a run reference - only appears when a command was interrupted mid-way"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:151
msgid "How verify, file, and export choose a revision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:153
msgid ""
"Most commands start from the visible filing target and then choose the "
"relevant calculation revision under that work unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:156
msgid ""
"Verification defaults to the current draft revision; run it with `aeat "
"app modelo work verify` (the chain sequence above runs it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:159
msgid "Local filing defaults to the current verified revision:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:164
msgid ""
"`work file` records a local filed marker. It does not submit anything to "
"AEAT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:166
msgid ""
"Export defaults to the filed revision if one exists. Otherwise, it uses "
"the current verified revision; run it with `aeat app modelo export` (the "
"chain sequence above runs it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:170
msgid ""
"Export refuses a plain draft. The upload file is the artefact that leaves"
" the tool for AEAT, so it is built only from a revision that passed the "
"completeness check (or one already recorded as filed) - the gate that "
"stops an incomplete or inconsistent draft from becoming a filing by "
"accident."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:175
msgid ""
"The `.boe` extension is a naming convention. The tool writes the file to "
"the `--output` path you choose and always produces a fixed-width fichero-"
"BOE text file, whatever extension you give it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:179
msgid "Each command automatically picks the most appropriate saved calculation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:181
msgid "`verify` uses the latest draft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:182
msgid "`file` uses the latest verified draft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:183
msgid ""
"`export` uses whichever was marked as filed; if none was filed, it uses "
"the verified draft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:186
msgid ""
"If you need a different saved calculation, use `--select` with the "
"visible target:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/filing-spine.md:192
msgid "You can also pass exact IDs on commands that accept them:"
msgstr ""

